## 1. Project Overview

### What Is This Project?

The **Discord Clip Submission System** is a full-stack, TypeScript-based application that lets content clippers submit video files to a company through a two-component system: a **Discord Bot** and a **Web Submission Portal**. The two components communicate with each other via an internal REST API server, all running as a single Node.js process.

### What Problem Does It Solve?

Content clipping companies typically receive clip submissions through informal Discord DMs, file-sharing services, or manual channels. This causes:

- No central record-keeping or tracking of who submitted what
- Discord's hard 10MB (free) / 25MB (Nitro) file attachment limit blocking real video files
- No enforcement of who is allowed to submit (role gating)
- No protection against spam (rate limiting)
- No standardized metadata collection (clip type, description)

This system solves all of the above by replacing ad-hoc submissions with a structured, auditable, gated workflow.

### Who Are the Users?

| Role | Description |
|---|---|
| **Clipper** | A Discord server member with the `Clipper` role who submits video clips |
| **Administrator** | A Discord server admin who runs `/setup-portal` to deploy the bot into a channel |
| **System Operator** | The person running `npm run dev` on the host machine |

